such as the right to be left alone most of the time, and maybe even
offered food if they were lucky.  But voluntary rights are not built upon
as firm a foundation as rights that have been fought for.  If a new road
was planned, I'd support chopping their trees down, and if some useful
experiment upon squirrels was proposed to help solve the problem of human
disease and aging I'd certainly be in favour, too.  Of course, things
should be made as painless as possible for the squirrels.  

